<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises prices for four grades of cotton.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises prices for four grades of cotton.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian exporters raised export prices for four grades of cotton but kept prices for the remaining grades unchanged, the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The association said prices for Giza 76, Giza 70 and Giza 77 were raised by two centilibre (U.S. cents per lb). Giza 75 prices were increased by three centilibres.</p>
<p>The prices in centilibres, valid until 2200 GMT December 21 are (previous week's prices in brackets):</p>
<p>	     FG/EX    FG+1/4     FG     FG-1/4    G/FG    G+3/8</p>
<p> Giza 76   176.0    170.0    164.0    158.0    152.0    149.0</p>
<p>	    (174.0    168.0    162.0    156.0    150.0    147.0)</p>
<p> Giza 70   169.0    163.0    157.0    151.0    145.0    142.0</p>
<p>	    (167.0    161.0    155.0    149.0    143.0    140.0)</p>
<p> Giza 77   164.0    158.0    152.0    146.0    140.0    137.0</p>
<p>	    (162.0    156.0    150.0    144.0    138.0    135.0)</p>
<p> Giza 75   139.0    133.0    127.0    121.0    115.0    112.0</p>
<p>	    (136.0    130.0    124.0    118.0    112.0    109.0)</p>
<p> Giza 85   131.0    125.0    119.0    113.0    107.0    104.0</p>
<p>	    (131.0    125.0    119.0    113.0    107.0    104.0)</p>
<p> Giza 83   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p> Giza 80   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p>Note - FG/EX = fully good/excellent, G/FG = good/fully good</p>
<p>-- Mona Eltahawy +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
